Aim: To simulate a voltage-series (series-shunt) feedback amplifier using MATLAB, measure

Input resistance with feedback (Rif)

Output resistance with feedback (Rof)

Voltage gain with feedback (Avf)

Bandwidth of the amplifier

and comment on the results.

Theory: Feedback amplifiers are widely used in electronic circuits to improve performance. In a voltage-series feedback configuration (also called series shunt feedbacky

The output voltage is sampled and fed back in series with the input.

The feedback increases the input resistance (Rif) and decreases the output resistance (Rof).

The overall gain with feedback (Avf) is reduced compared to the open-loop gain but becomes more stable.

The bandwidth of the amplifier increases due to negative feedback.

